1
00:00:00,989 --> 00:00:08,629
Chapter 24 As I rose and dressed, I thought over what had happened,

2
00:00:09,309 --> 00:00:10,910
and wondered if it were a dream.

3
00:00:11,870 --> 00:00:16,470
I could not be certain of the reality till I had seen Mr. Rochester again,

4
00:00:17,309 --> 00:00:20,169
and heard him renew his words of love and promise.

5
00:00:21,050 --> 00:00:24,065
While arranging my hair, I looked at my face

6
00:00:24,065 --> 00:00:27,311
in the glass, and felt it was no longer plain.

7
00:00:28,349 --> 00:00:34,110
There was hope in its aspect and life in its color, and my eyes seemed as if they

8
00:00:34,110 --> 00:00:40,230
had beheld the fount of fruition, and borrowed beams from the lustrous ripple.

9
00:00:40,930 --> 00:00:46,129
I had often been unwilling to look at my master, because I feared he could not be

10
00:00:46,131 --> 00:00:51,355
pleased at my look, but I was sure I might lift my face

11
00:00:51,357 --> 00:00:55,150
to his now, and not cool his affection by its expression.

12
00:00:56,230 --> 00:01:01,050
I took a plain but clean and light sum -address from my drawer and put it on.

13
00:01:02,110 --> 00:01:05,652
It seemed no attire had ever so well become me,

14
00:01:05,652 --> 00:01:09,730
because none had I ever worn in so blissful a mood.

15
00:01:10,610 --> 00:01:16,449
I was not surprised when I ran down into the hall, to see that a brilliant June

16
00:01:16,451 --> 00:01:21,809
morning had succeeded to the tempest of the night, and to feel through the open

17
00:01:21,811 --> 00:01:26,489
glass door the breathing of a fresh and fragrant breeze.

18
00:01:27,610 --> 00:01:30,389
Nature must be gladsome when I was so happy.

19
00:01:31,709 --> 00:01:37,790
A beggar woman and her little boy, pale ragged objects both, were coming up

20
00:01:37,790 --> 00:01:43,069
the walk, and I ran down and gave them all the money I happened to have in my purse.

21
00:01:44,029 --> 00:01:48,830
Some three or four shillings, good or bad, they must partake of my jubilee.

22
00:01:49,470 --> 00:01:53,940
The rook's cord, and believe the bird's sang, but nothing

23
00:01:53,942 --> 00:01:58,250
was so merry or so musical as my own rejoicing heart.

24
00:01:59,650 --> 00:02:03,650
Mrs. Fairfax surprised me by looking out of the window with a sad countenance and

25
00:02:03,650 --> 00:02:08,290
saying gravely, Miss Air, will you come to breakfast?

26
00:02:09,610 --> 00:02:14,629
During the meal she was quiet and cool, but I could not understive her then.

27
00:02:15,589 --> 00:02:19,650
I must wait for my master to give explanations and so must she.

28
00:02:20,389 --> 00:02:23,290
I ate what I could, and then I hastened upstairs.

29
00:02:24,330 --> 00:02:26,610
I met Adele leaving the schoolroom.

30
00:02:27,870 --> 00:02:28,870
Where are you going?

31
00:02:29,529 --> 00:02:30,529
It is time for lessons.

32
00:02:31,550 --> 00:02:33,930
Mr. Rochester has sent me away to the nursery.

33
00:02:35,230 --> 00:02:36,230
Where is he?

34
00:02:36,870 --> 00:02:41,589
In there, pointing to the apartment she had left, and I went in.

35
00:02:42,129 --> 00:02:43,129
And there he stood.

36
00:02:44,050 --> 00:02:46,069
Come and bid me good morning, said he.

37
00:02:47,690 --> 00:02:53,110
I gladly advanced, and it was not merely a cold word now, or even a shake of the hand

38
00:02:53,110 --> 00:02:56,069
that I received, but an embrace and a kiss.

39
00:02:56,849 --> 00:02:57,889
It seemed natural.

40
00:02:58,730 --> 00:03:02,470
It seemed genial to be so well loved, so caressed by him.

41
00:03:03,449 --> 00:03:07,470
Jane, you look blooming and smiling and pretty, said he.

42
00:03:08,230 --> 00:03:09,430
Truly pretty this morning.

43
00:03:10,430 --> 00:03:12,190
Is this my pale little elf?

44
00:03:13,089 --> 00:03:14,589
Is this my mustard seed?

45
00:03:15,470 --> 00:03:20,709
This little sunny-faced girl with the dimpled cheek and rosy lips, the satin

46
00:03:20,711 --> 00:03:23,550
smooth hazel hair, and the radiant hazel eyes?

47
00:03:24,669 --> 00:03:28,309
I had green eyes, reader, but you must excuse the mistake.

48
00:03:28,989 --> 00:03:30,610
For him they were new-dyed, I suppose.

49
00:03:31,629 --> 00:03:33,069
It is Jane air, sir.

50
00:03:34,190 --> 00:03:35,389
Soon to be Jane Rochester.

51
00:03:36,430 --> 00:03:39,889
He added, in four weeks, Janet, not a day more.

52
00:03:40,209 --> 00:03:41,209
Do you hear that?

53
00:03:42,110 --> 00:03:43,110
I did.

54
00:03:43,510 --> 00:03:45,709
And I could not quite comprehend it.

55
00:03:46,330 --> 00:03:47,330
It made me giddy.

56
00:03:48,209 --> 00:03:53,230
The feeling, the announcement sent through me, was something stronger than was

57
00:03:53,230 --> 00:03:56,769
consistent with joy, something that smote and stunned.

58
00:03:57,870 --> 00:03:59,129
It was, I think, almost fear.

59
00:03:59,949 --> 00:04:02,690
You blushed, and now you are white, Jane.

60
00:04:03,510 --> 00:04:04,510
What is that for?

61
00:04:05,470 --> 00:04:07,169
Because you gave me a new name.

62
00:04:08,190 --> 00:04:10,730
Jane Rochester, and it seems so strange.

63
00:04:11,610 --> 00:04:14,169
Yes, Mrs. Rochester, said he.

64
00:04:14,769 --> 00:04:15,809
Young Mrs. Rochester.

65
00:04:16,569 --> 00:04:18,389
Fairfax Rochester's girl, bride.

66
00:04:20,150 --> 00:04:21,650
It can never be, sir.

67
00:04:22,209 --> 00:04:23,230
It does not sound likely.

68
00:04:24,330 --> 00:04:27,750
Human beings never enjoy complete happiness in this world.

69
00:04:28,449 --> 00:04:31,790
I was not born for a different destiny to the rest of my species.

70
00:04:33,110 --> 00:04:38,194
To imagine such a lot beforeling me as a fairytale, a

71
00:04:38,196 --> 00:04:42,910
daydream, which I can and will realize, I shall begin today.

72
00:04:43,949 --> 00:04:48,529
This morning, I wrote to my banker in London, to send me certain jewels he has

73
00:04:48,531 --> 00:04:51,769
in his keeping, heirlooms for the ladies of Thornfield.

74
00:04:52,809 --> 00:04:57,589
In a day or two, I hope to pour them into your lap, for every privilege,

75
00:04:57,989 --> 00:05:02,150
every attention shall be yours, that I would accord a peer's daughter,

76
00:05:02,849 --> 00:05:04,169
if about to marry her.

77
00:05:05,209 --> 00:05:08,209
Oh, sir, never rain jewels.

78
00:05:09,069 --> 00:05:10,769
I don't like to hear them spoken of.

79
00:05:11,650 --> 00:05:14,650
Jewels for Jane heir sounds unnatural and strange.

80
00:05:15,449 --> 00:05:16,849
I would rather not have them.

81
00:05:18,290 --> 00:05:23,269
I will myself put the diamond chain round your neck, and the circuit on your

82
00:05:23,271 --> 00:05:29,190
forehead, which it will become, for nature at least, has stamped her

83
00:05:29,190 --> 00:05:34,169
patent of nobility on this brow, Jane, and I will clasp the bracelets on

84
00:05:34,171 --> 00:05:38,569
these fine wrists, and load these fairy -like fingers with rings.

85
00:05:39,650 --> 00:05:42,866
No, no, sir, think of other subjects, and

86
00:05:42,866 --> 00:05:47,071
speak of other things, and in another strain.

87
00:05:47,889 --> 00:05:50,230
Don't address me as if I were a beauty.

88
00:05:50,989 --> 00:05:53,809
I am your plain, quaker-ish, governess.

89
00:05:54,610 --> 00:05:59,949
You are a beauty in my eyes, and a beauty just after the desire of my heart,

90
00:06:00,730 --> 00:06:02,010
delicate and aerial.

91
00:06:03,169 --> 00:06:04,970
Puny and insignificant, you mean.

92
00:06:05,750 --> 00:06:10,330
You are dreaming, sir, or you are sneering for God's sake, don't be ironical.

93
00:06:12,069 --> 00:06:15,269
I will make the world acknowledge you a beauty, too.

94
00:06:16,169 --> 00:06:17,169
He went on.

95
00:06:17,389 --> 00:06:22,989
While I really became uneasy at the strain he had adopted, because I felt he was

96
00:06:22,991 --> 00:06:25,730
either deluding himself for trying to delude me.

97
00:06:27,370 --> 00:06:33,889
I will attire my Jane in satan and lace, and she shall have roses in her hair,

98
00:06:34,610 --> 00:06:38,550
and I will cover the head I love best with a priceless veil.

99
00:06:39,769 --> 00:06:41,870
And then you won't know me, sir.

100
00:06:42,690 --> 00:06:46,232
And I shall not be your Jane heir any longer, but an

101
00:06:46,233 --> 00:06:50,910
ape in a Harlequin's jacket, a jay in borrowed plumes.

102
00:06:51,870 --> 00:06:56,684
I would as soon see you, Mr. Rochester, tricked out in

103
00:06:56,684 --> 00:07:00,610
stage trappings as myself clad in a court-lady's robe.

104
00:07:01,430 --> 00:07:05,010
And I don't call you handsome, sir, though I love you most dearly,

105
00:07:05,370 --> 00:07:08,750
far too dearly to flatter you, don't flatter me.

106
00:07:09,790 --> 00:07:14,190
He pursued his theme, however, without noticing my deprecation.

107
00:07:15,610 --> 00:07:18,999
This very day I shall take you in the carriage to

108
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:22,230
Milcoat, and you must choose some dresses for yourself.

109
00:07:23,209 --> 00:07:26,089
I told you we shall be married in four weeks.

110
00:07:26,989 --> 00:07:31,375
The wedding is to take place quietly in the church down

111
00:07:31,375 --> 00:07:35,370
below Yonder, and then I shall waft you away at once to town.

112
00:07:36,290 --> 00:07:41,610
After a brief stay there, I shall bear my treasure to regions near the sun,

113
00:07:42,269 --> 00:07:46,241
to French vineyards and Italian plains, and she shall

114
00:07:46,241 --> 00:07:50,410
see whatever is famous in old story and in modern record.

115
00:07:51,470 --> 00:07:55,944
She shall taste, too, of the life of cities, and she shall

116
00:07:55,946 --> 00:07:59,110
learn to value herself by just comparison with others.

117
00:08:00,169 --> 00:08:02,629
Shall I travel, and with you, sir?

118
00:08:03,930 --> 00:08:10,010
You shall sojourn at Paris, Rome, and Naples, at Florence, Venice, and Vienna.

119
00:08:10,150 --> 00:08:14,190
All the ground I have wandered over shall be retrodden by you.

120
00:08:15,790 --> 00:08:20,129
Wherever I stamped my hoof, your silph's foot shall step also.

121
00:08:21,069 --> 00:08:24,989
Ten years since, I flew through Europe half-mad,

122
00:08:24,991 --> 00:08:28,451
with disgust, hate, and rage as my companions.

123
00:08:29,169 --> 00:08:35,491
Now I shall revisit it, healed and cleansed, with a very angel as my comforter.

124
00:08:36,150 --> 00:08:37,769
I laughed at him as he said this.

125
00:08:38,629 --> 00:08:43,349
I am not an angel, I asserted, and I will not be one till I die.

126
00:08:43,970 --> 00:08:45,129
I will be myself.

127
00:08:46,349 --> 00:08:51,110
Mr. Rochester, you must neither expect nor exec anything celestial of me.

128
00:08:51,930 --> 00:08:55,415
For you will not get it, any more than I shall

129
00:08:55,417 --> 00:08:59,230
get it of you, which I do not at all anticipate.

130
00:09:00,150 --> 00:09:01,910
What do you anticipate of me?

131
00:09:03,589 --> 00:09:09,029
For a little while, you will perhaps be as you are now, a very little while,

132
00:09:09,709 --> 00:09:15,050
and then you will turn cool, and then you will be capricious, and then you will be

133
00:09:15,050 --> 00:09:18,489
stern, and I shall have much ado to please you.

134
00:09:19,110 --> 00:09:23,269
But when you get well used to me, you will perhaps like me again.

135
00:09:24,230 --> 00:09:26,510
Like me I say, not love me.

136
00:09:27,309 --> 00:09:31,370
I suppose your love will effervesce in six months or less.

137
00:09:32,650 --> 00:09:36,292
I have observed in books written by men, that period

138
00:09:36,292 --> 00:09:39,809
assigned as the farthest to which a husband's ardor extends.

139
00:09:40,830 --> 00:09:44,514
Yet, after all, as a friend and companion, I hope

140
00:09:44,514 --> 00:09:48,029
never to become quite distasteful to my dear master.

141
00:09:49,769 --> 00:09:54,029
Distasteful, and like you again, I think I shall like you again,

142
00:09:54,290 --> 00:09:58,650
and yet again, and I will make you confess I do not only like, but love you,

143
00:09:59,089 --> 00:10:01,930
with truth, fervor, constancy.

144
00:10:03,169 --> 00:10:05,230
Yet are you not capricious, sir?

145
00:10:06,709 --> 00:10:10,726
To women who please me only by their faces, I am the very

146
00:10:10,728 --> 00:10:13,930
devil when I find out they have neither the souls nor hearts.

147
00:10:14,769 --> 00:10:19,610
When they open to me a perspective of flatness, triviality, and perhaps in

148
00:10:19,610 --> 00:10:24,870
versility, coarseness, and ill-temper, but to the clear eye and eloquent tongue,

149
00:10:25,529 --> 00:10:29,690
to the soul made of fire, and the character that bends but does not break,

150
00:10:30,389 --> 00:10:37,150
at once supple and stable, tractable and consistent, I am ever tender and true.

151
00:10:38,750 --> 00:10:41,349
How do you ever experience such a character, sir?

152
00:10:42,050 --> 00:10:43,269
Did you ever love such in one?

153
00:10:44,050 --> 00:10:48,625
I love it now, but before me, if I indeed, in any respect

154
00:10:48,627 --> 00:10:52,910
come up to your difficult standard, I never met your likeness.

155
00:10:53,330 --> 00:10:56,650
Jane, you please me, and you master me.

156
00:10:57,550 --> 00:11:03,389
You seem to submit, and I like the sense of play and see you impart, and while I am

157
00:11:03,391 --> 00:11:05,792
twining the soft, silken skein' round my

158
00:11:05,794 --> 00:11:09,771
finger, it sends a thrill up my arm to my heart.

159
00:11:10,290 --> 00:11:15,889
I am influenced, conquered, and the influence is sweeter than I can express,

160
00:11:16,650 --> 00:11:20,849
and the conquest I undergo has a witchery beyond any triumph I can win.

161
00:11:21,690 --> 00:11:23,069
Why do you smile, Jane?

162
00:11:23,949 --> 00:11:27,209
What does that inexplicable, that uncanny turn of countenance mean?

163
00:11:27,949 --> 00:11:29,150
I was thinking, sir.

164
00:11:29,889 --> 00:11:32,370
You will excuse the idea it was in voluntary.

165
00:11:32,949 --> 00:11:36,349
I was thinking of Hercules and Samson with their charmers.

166
00:11:37,209 --> 00:11:40,830
You were, you little elfish, hush, sir.

167
00:11:41,769 --> 00:11:47,491
You don't talk very wisely just now, any more than those gentlemen acted very wisely.

168
00:11:47,949 --> 00:11:53,169
However, had they been married, they would no doubt by their severity as

169
00:11:53,171 --> 00:11:58,430
husbands have made up for their softness as suitors, and so will you, I fear.

170
00:12:00,690 --> 00:12:04,069
I wonder how you will answer me a year hence?

171
00:12:04,669 --> 00:12:08,690
Should I ask a favor it does not suit your convenience or pleasure to grant?

172
00:12:10,389 --> 00:12:13,709
Ask me something now, Janet, the least thing.

173
00:12:14,589 --> 00:12:16,050
I desire to be entreated.

174
00:12:16,830 --> 00:12:17,830
Indeed, I will, sir.

175
00:12:18,370 --> 00:12:20,010
I have my petition already.

176
00:12:21,029 --> 00:12:22,029
Speak.

177
00:12:22,309 --> 00:12:27,250
But if you look up and smile with that countenance, I shall swear concession

178
00:12:27,250 --> 00:12:30,750
before I know to what, and that will make a fool of me.

179
00:12:32,029 --> 00:12:33,330
Not at all, sir.

180
00:12:33,970 --> 00:12:35,370
I ask only this.

181
00:12:36,330 --> 00:12:39,769
Don't send for the jewels, and don't crown me with roses.

182
00:12:40,650 --> 00:12:43,173
You might as well put a border of gold lace around

183
00:12:43,173 --> 00:12:45,750
that plain pocket hankerchief you have there.

184
00:12:47,230 --> 00:12:49,870
I might as well guild refined gold.

185
00:12:51,029 --> 00:12:52,029
I know it.

186
00:12:52,629 --> 00:12:55,230
Your request is granted then, for the time.

187
00:12:55,230 --> 00:12:58,338
I will remind the order I dispatched to my

188
00:12:58,339 --> 00:13:01,250
banker, but you have not yet asked for anything.

189
00:13:01,910 --> 00:13:03,529
You have prayed a gift to be withdrawn.

190
00:13:04,169 --> 00:13:05,169
Try again.

191
00:13:06,550 --> 00:13:07,550
Well then, sir.

192
00:13:08,290 --> 00:13:13,690
Have the goodness to gratify my curiosity, which is much peaked on one point.

193
00:13:15,250 --> 00:13:16,430
He looked disturbed.

194
00:13:17,690 --> 00:13:18,690
What?

195
00:13:18,870 --> 00:13:19,870
What?

196
00:13:19,930 --> 00:13:20,930
He said hastily.

197
00:13:21,610 --> 00:13:23,430
Curiosity is a dangerous petition.

198
00:13:24,150 --> 00:13:29,330
It is well I have not taken a vow to accord every request, but there can be no

199
00:13:29,330 --> 00:13:31,209
danger in complying with this, sir.

200
00:13:32,250 --> 00:13:33,250
utter it, Jane.

201
00:13:33,769 --> 00:13:36,792
But I wish that instead of a mere inquiry into

202
00:13:36,792 --> 00:13:40,091
perhaps a secret, it was a wish for half my estate.

203
00:13:41,330 --> 00:13:45,669
Now, King Ahasuerus, what do I want with half your estate?

204
00:13:46,489 --> 00:13:48,949
Do you think I am a due usurer?

205
00:13:49,669 --> 00:13:51,449
Seeking good investment in land?

206
00:13:52,750 --> 00:13:55,010
I would much rather have all your confidence.

207
00:13:56,150 --> 00:14:01,430
You will not exclude me from your confidence if you admit me to your heart.

208
00:14:03,089 --> 00:14:06,989
You are welcome to all my confidence that is worth having, Jane.

209
00:14:08,129 --> 00:14:11,290
But for God's sake, don't desire a useless burden.

210
00:14:12,169 --> 00:14:13,169
Don't long for poison.

211
00:14:13,989 --> 00:14:16,569
Don't turn out a downright eve on my hands.

212
00:14:18,389 --> 00:14:19,669
Why not, sir?

213
00:14:20,690 --> 00:14:23,874
You have just been telling me how much you like to be

214
00:14:23,875 --> 00:14:27,629
conquered and how pleasant over persuasion is to you.

215
00:14:28,930 --> 00:14:33,330
Don't you think I had better take advantage of the confession and begin in

216
00:14:33,330 --> 00:14:36,305
coax and in treat, even cry and be sulky if

217
00:14:36,307 --> 00:14:40,250
necessary for the sake of mere essay of my power?

218
00:14:40,730 --> 00:14:46,330
I dare you to any such experiment, encroach, presume, and the game is up.

219
00:14:47,690 --> 00:14:48,690
Is it, sir?

220
00:14:49,370 --> 00:14:52,050
You soon give in, how stern you look now.

221
00:14:53,330 --> 00:14:57,669
Your eyebrows have become as thick as my finger, and your forehead resembles what

222
00:14:57,671 --> 00:15:04,309
in some very astonishing poetry I once saw styled a blue piled thunder loft.

223
00:15:05,190 --> 00:15:08,069
That will be your married look, sir, I suppose.

224
00:15:09,050 --> 00:15:14,650
If that will be your married look, I, as a Christian, will soon give up the

225
00:15:14,650 --> 00:15:18,069
notion of consorting with a mere sprite or salamander.

226
00:15:18,809 --> 00:15:22,269
But what had you to ask, thing, out with it?

227
00:15:23,269 --> 00:15:26,779
There, you are less than civil now, and I like

228
00:15:26,781 --> 00:15:29,891
rudeness a great deal better than flattery.

229
00:15:30,410 --> 00:15:32,650
I had rather be a thing than an angel.

230
00:15:33,489 --> 00:15:34,970
This is what I have to ask.

231
00:15:35,989 --> 00:15:40,209
Why did you take such pains to make me believe you wish to marry Miss Ingram?

232
00:15:41,410 --> 00:15:42,430
Is that all?

233
00:15:43,069 --> 00:15:44,430
Thank God it is no worse.

234
00:15:45,650 --> 00:15:51,230
And now he unknit his black brows, looked down, smiling at me, and stroked my

235
00:15:51,230 --> 00:15:55,150
hair, as if well pleased at seeing a danger averted.

236
00:15:56,389 --> 00:16:00,457
I think I may confess, he continued, even although

237
00:16:00,459 --> 00:16:03,470
I should make you a little indignant, Jane.

238
00:16:04,209 --> 00:16:08,529
And I have seen what a fire spirit you can be when you are indignant.

239
00:16:09,510 --> 00:16:13,930
You glowed in the cool moonlight last night, when you mutinyed against fate,

240
00:16:14,730 --> 00:16:16,569
and claimed your rank as my equal.

241
00:16:17,470 --> 00:16:22,330
Janet, by the by, it was you who made me the offer.

242
00:16:23,650 --> 00:16:28,410
Of course I did, but to the point of you please sir, Miss Ingram.

243
00:16:29,430 --> 00:16:35,389
Well, I feigned courtship of Miss Ingram, because I wish to render you as madly in

244
00:16:35,391 --> 00:16:40,389
love with me as I was with you, and I knew jealousy would be the best ally

245
00:16:40,391 --> 00:16:42,870
I could call in for the furtherance of that end.

246
00:16:44,050 --> 00:16:49,510
Excellent, now you are small, not one wit bigger than the end of my little finger.

247
00:16:50,339 --> 00:16:54,129
It was a burning shame and a scandalous disgrace to act in that way.

248
00:16:54,970 --> 00:16:57,910
Did you think nothing of Miss Ingram's feelings, sir?

249
00:16:59,730 --> 00:17:04,849
Her feelings are concentrated in one, pride, and that needs humbling.

250
00:17:05,809 --> 00:17:07,029
Were you jealous, Jane?

251
00:17:08,730 --> 00:17:09,989
Never mind, Mr. Rochester.

252
00:17:10,830 --> 00:17:13,269
It is in no way interesting to you to know that.

253
00:17:14,269 --> 00:17:16,069
Answer me truly once more.

254
00:17:16,970 --> 00:17:20,790
Do you think Miss Ingram will not suffer from your dishonest cockatry?

255
00:17:21,569 --> 00:17:23,290
Won't she feel forsaken and deserted?

256
00:17:25,430 --> 00:17:26,430
Impossible.

257
00:17:27,050 --> 00:17:32,970
When I told you how she, on the contrary, deserted me, the idea of my insolvency

258
00:17:32,970 --> 00:17:36,129
cooled or rather extinguished her flame in a moment.

259
00:17:37,349 --> 00:17:40,910
You have a curious, designing mind, Mr. Rochester.

260
00:17:41,830 --> 00:17:45,089
I'm afraid your principles on some points are eccentric.

261
00:17:46,269 --> 00:17:48,849
My principles were never trained, Jane.

262
00:17:49,730 --> 00:17:52,589
They may have grown a little awry for want of attention.

263
00:17:53,970 --> 00:18:00,589
Once again, seriously, may I enjoy the great good that has been vouchsafed to me,

264
00:18:01,089 --> 00:18:03,817
without fearing that anyone else is suffering

265
00:18:03,817 --> 00:18:06,911
the bitter pain I myself felt a while ago.

266
00:18:07,510 --> 00:18:09,930
That you may, my good little girl.

267
00:18:10,730 --> 00:18:15,410
There is not another being in the world has the same pure love for me as yourself.

268
00:18:16,389 --> 00:18:21,769
For I lay that pleasant action to my soul, Jane, a belief in your affection.

269
00:18:23,470 --> 00:18:26,550
I turn my lips to the hand that lay on my shoulder.

270
00:18:27,669 --> 00:18:29,309
I loved him very much.

271
00:18:30,029 --> 00:18:31,669
More than I could trust myself to say.

272
00:18:32,529 --> 00:18:34,349
More than words had power to express.

273
00:18:35,550 --> 00:18:38,089
Ask something more, he said presently.

274
00:18:38,610 --> 00:18:41,870
It is my delight to be entreated and to yield.

275
00:18:42,910 --> 00:18:45,129
I was again ready with my request.

276
00:18:46,529 --> 00:18:49,089
Communicate your intentions to Mrs. Fairfax, sir.

277
00:18:50,010 --> 00:18:53,949
She saw me with you last night in the hall and she was shocked.

278
00:18:54,849 --> 00:18:57,129
Give her some explanation before I see her again.

279
00:18:58,089 --> 00:19:00,970
It pains me to be misjudged by so good a woman.

280
00:19:02,610 --> 00:19:06,349
Go to your room and put on your bonnet, he replied.

281
00:19:07,269 --> 00:19:12,769
I mean you to accompany me to Milkut this morning, and while you prepare for the

282
00:19:12,771 --> 00:19:16,349
drive, I will enlighten the old lady's understanding.

283
00:19:17,250 --> 00:19:23,451
Did she think Janet, you had given the world for love and considered it well lost?

284
00:19:24,449 --> 00:19:28,169
I believe she thought I had forgotten my station and yours, sir.

285
00:19:29,169 --> 00:19:30,169
Station.

286
00:19:30,489 --> 00:19:31,489
Station.

287
00:19:31,669 --> 00:19:34,667
Your station is in my heart and on the next of

288
00:19:34,667 --> 00:19:38,010
those who would insult you now or hereafter.

289
00:19:38,129 --> 00:19:39,129
Go.

290
00:19:39,669 --> 00:19:45,889
I was soon dressed, and when I heard Mr. Rochester quit, Mrs. Fairfax's parlour,

291
00:19:46,430 --> 00:19:47,690
I hurried down to it.

292
00:19:48,370 --> 00:19:51,250
The old lady had been reading her morning portion of scripture.

293
00:19:52,089 --> 00:19:54,550
The lesson for the day, her Bible lay open

294
00:19:54,552 --> 00:19:58,571
before her, and her spectacles were upon it.

295
00:19:58,849 --> 00:20:04,930
Her occupation, suspended by Mr. Rochester's announcement, seemed now forgotten.

296
00:20:05,209 --> 00:20:09,213
Her eyes fixed on the blank wall opposite, expressed the

297
00:20:09,213 --> 00:20:13,809
surprise of a quiet mind stirred by unwanted tidings.

298
00:20:14,589 --> 00:20:16,949
Seeing me, she roused herself.

299
00:20:17,750 --> 00:20:22,489
She made a sort of effort to smile and framed a few words of congratulation.

300
00:20:23,190 --> 00:20:27,569
But the smile expired, and the sentence was abandoned unfinished.

301
00:20:28,690 --> 00:20:33,550
She put up her spectacles, shut the Bible, and pushed her chair back from the table.

302
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:37,489
I feel so astonished, she began.

303
00:20:38,330 --> 00:20:40,709
I hardly know what to say to you, Miss Ayer.

304
00:20:41,470 --> 00:20:44,050
I have surely not been dreaming, have I?

305
00:20:44,830 --> 00:20:47,053
Sometimes I have fall asleep when I'm sitting

306
00:20:47,055 --> 00:20:49,771
alone and fancy things that have never happened.

307
00:20:50,989 --> 00:20:55,730
It has seemed to me more than once when I've been in a dose, that my dear husband,

308
00:20:56,309 --> 00:21:02,430
who died 15 years since, has come in and sat down beside me, and that I've even

309
00:21:02,430 --> 00:21:06,769
heard him call me by my name, Alice, as he used to do.

310
00:21:08,650 --> 00:21:11,529
Now, can you tell me whether it is actually true

311
00:21:11,531 --> 00:21:14,211
that Mr. Rochester has asked you to marry him?

312
00:21:14,769 --> 00:21:18,911
Don't laugh at me, but I really thought he came in here five

313
00:21:18,911 --> 00:21:21,910
minutes ago and said that in a month you would be his wife.

314
00:21:23,269 --> 00:21:25,569
He has said the same thing to me, I replied.

315
00:21:26,190 --> 00:21:27,190
He has.

316
00:21:27,269 --> 00:21:28,269
Do you believe him?

317
00:21:28,510 --> 00:21:29,690
Have you accepted him?

318
00:21:30,750 --> 00:21:31,750
Yes.

319
00:21:31,949 --> 00:21:33,349
She looked at me bewildered.

320
00:21:34,410 --> 00:21:35,750
I could never have thought it.

321
00:21:36,309 --> 00:21:37,470
He is a proud man.

322
00:21:38,290 --> 00:21:42,709
All the Rochester's were proud, and his father at least liked money.

323
00:21:43,629 --> 00:21:45,370
He too has always been called careful.

324
00:21:45,989 --> 00:21:47,309
He means to marry you.

325
00:21:48,930 --> 00:21:49,930
He tells me so.

326
00:21:50,629 --> 00:21:52,250
She surveyed my whole person.

327
00:21:53,269 --> 00:21:55,875
In her eyes, I read that they had their found

328
00:21:55,875 --> 00:21:59,050
no charm, powerful enough to solve the enigma.

329
00:21:59,910 --> 00:22:05,389
It passes me, she continued, but no doubt it is true since you say so.

330
00:22:06,169 --> 00:22:08,269
How it will answer, I cannot tell.

331
00:22:09,290 --> 00:22:10,349
I really don't know.

332
00:22:11,089 --> 00:22:15,461
A quality of position and fortune is often advisable in such

333
00:22:15,461 --> 00:22:18,970
cases, and there are 20 years of difference in your ages.

334
00:22:19,769 --> 00:22:21,190
He might almost be your father.

335
00:22:22,730 --> 00:22:26,949
No, indeed Mrs. Fairfax exclaimed I, nettleed.

336
00:22:27,529 --> 00:22:29,529
He is nothing like my father.

337
00:22:30,610 --> 00:22:34,110
No one who saw us together would suppose it for an instant.

338
00:22:35,309 --> 00:22:40,489
Mr. Rochester looks as young and is as young as some men at five and twenty.

339
00:22:41,610 --> 00:22:43,970
Is it really for love he is going to marry you?

340
00:22:44,769 --> 00:22:45,769
She asked.

341
00:22:46,510 --> 00:22:52,169
I was so hurt by her coldness and skepticism that the tears rose to my eyes.

342
00:22:52,830 --> 00:22:59,309
I'm sorry to grieve you pursued the widow, but you are so young and so little

343
00:22:59,311 --> 00:23:03,529
acquainted with men, I wished to put you on your guard.

344
00:23:04,370 --> 00:23:07,370
It is an old saying that all is not gold that glitters.

345
00:23:07,989 --> 00:23:11,997
And in this case, I do fear there will be something

346
00:23:11,999 --> 00:23:16,089
found to be different to what either you or I expect.

347
00:23:17,389 --> 00:23:18,389
Why?

348
00:23:18,529 --> 00:23:19,529
Am I a monster?

349
00:23:20,230 --> 00:23:21,230
I said.

350
00:23:21,470 --> 00:23:25,050
Is it impossible that Mr. Rochester should have a sincere affection for me?

351
00:23:30,069 --> 00:23:38,069
No, you are very well, and much improved of late, and Mr. Rochester, head of his.

352
00:23:38,930 --> 00:23:44,510
There are times when, for your sake, I have been a little uneasy at his marked

353
00:23:44,510 --> 00:23:48,987
preference, and have wished to put you on your guard, but

354
00:23:48,987 --> 00:23:52,750
I did not like to suggest even the possibility of wrong.

355
00:23:53,809 --> 00:23:59,230
I knew such an idea would shock, perhaps offend you, and you were so

356
00:23:59,230 --> 00:24:02,809
discrete and so thoroughly modest and sensible.

357
00:24:03,529 --> 00:24:06,410
I hoped you might be trusted to protect yourself.

358
00:24:07,349 --> 00:24:12,190
Last night, I cannot tell you what I suffered when I sought all over the house

359
00:24:12,190 --> 00:24:18,690
and could find you nowhere, nor the master either, and then, at twelve o'clock,

360
00:24:19,349 --> 00:24:20,449
saw you come in with him.

361
00:24:22,150 --> 00:24:26,510
Well, never mind that now, I interrupted impatiently.

362
00:24:27,129 --> 00:24:28,910
It is enough that all was right.

363
00:24:30,389 --> 00:24:33,910
I hope all will be right in the end, she said,

364
00:24:33,911 --> 00:24:37,171
but believe me, you cannot be too careful.

365
00:24:38,150 --> 00:24:40,489
Try and keep Mr. Rochester at a distance.

366
00:24:41,449 --> 00:24:43,290
Distrust yourself as well as him.

367
00:24:44,669 --> 00:24:48,230
Gentleman in his station are not accustomed to marry their governesses.

368
00:24:49,730 --> 00:24:52,050
I was growing truly irritated.

369
00:24:52,889 --> 00:24:54,830
Happily, Adele ran in.

370
00:24:55,930 --> 00:24:56,930
Let me go.

371
00:24:57,269 --> 00:24:59,209
Let me go to Milkut, too, she cried.

372
00:25:00,349 --> 00:25:04,190
Mr. Rochester won't, though there is so much room in the new carriage,

373
00:25:04,849 --> 00:25:06,790
beg him to let me go, Mademoiselle.

374
00:25:08,230 --> 00:25:15,571
That I will, Adele, and I hastened away with her, glad to quit my gloomy monatrous.

375
00:25:16,569 --> 00:25:17,989
The carriage was ready.

376
00:25:18,769 --> 00:25:23,169
They were bringing it round to the front, and my master was pacing the pavement,

377
00:25:23,790 --> 00:25:26,029
pilot following him backwards and forwards.

378
00:25:27,349 --> 00:25:28,809
Adele may accompany us.

379
00:25:29,309 --> 00:25:30,309
May she not, sir.

380
00:25:31,449 --> 00:25:32,449
I told her no.

381
00:25:32,830 --> 00:25:33,870
I'll have no brats.

382
00:25:34,349 --> 00:25:35,349
I'll have only you.

383
00:25:36,790 --> 00:25:38,370
Do let her go, Mr. Rochester.

384
00:25:38,769 --> 00:25:40,669
If you please, it would be better.

385
00:25:41,750 --> 00:25:42,750
Not it.

386
00:25:42,870 --> 00:25:44,110
She will be a restraint.

387
00:25:44,110 --> 00:25:48,410
He was quite preemptory, both in look and voice.

388
00:25:49,269 --> 00:25:54,110
The chill of Mrs. Fairfax's warnings, and the damp of her doubts were upon me,

389
00:25:54,690 --> 00:25:59,190
something of unsubstantiality and uncertainty, had beset my hopes.

390
00:26:00,569 --> 00:26:03,389
I half lost the sense of power over him.

391
00:26:04,150 --> 00:26:08,089
I was about mechanically to obey him, without further remonstrance.

392
00:26:08,889 --> 00:26:13,169
But as he helped me into the carriage, he looked at my face.

393
00:26:14,389 --> 00:26:16,889
What is the matter, he asked?

394
00:26:17,809 --> 00:26:19,190
All the sunshine is gone.

395
00:26:20,089 --> 00:26:21,910
Do you really wish the band to go?

396
00:26:22,949 --> 00:26:25,230
Will it annoy you if she is left behind?

397
00:26:26,550 --> 00:26:28,430
I would far rather she went, sir.

398
00:26:29,449 --> 00:26:34,569
Then off for your bonnet, and back like a flash of lightning cried he to Adele.

399
00:26:35,470 --> 00:26:37,669
She obeyed him with what speed she might.

400
00:26:38,650 --> 00:26:43,769
After all, a single morning's interruption will not matter much, said he,

401
00:26:44,510 --> 00:26:50,410
when I mean shortly to claim you, your thoughts, conversation and company for life.

402
00:26:51,650 --> 00:26:55,610
Adele, when lifted in, commenced kissing me, by way

403
00:26:55,610 --> 00:26:58,911
of expressing her gratitude for my intercession.

404
00:26:59,809 --> 00:27:03,569
She was instantly stowed away into a corner on the other side of him.

405
00:27:04,349 --> 00:27:09,910
She then peeped round to where I sat, so stern a neighbour was too restrictive.

406
00:27:10,669 --> 00:27:16,129
To him, in his present, fractious mood, she dared whisper no observations,

407
00:27:16,709 --> 00:27:18,690
nor ask of him any information.

408
00:27:20,029 --> 00:27:22,489
Let her come to me, I entreated.

409
00:27:23,230 --> 00:27:25,250
She will perhaps trouble you, sir.

410
00:27:25,930 --> 00:27:27,790
There is plenty of room on this side.

411
00:27:28,870 --> 00:27:31,169
He handed her over as if she had been a lap dog.

412
00:27:32,269 --> 00:27:36,449
I'll send her to school yet, he said, but now he was smiling.

413
00:27:37,589 --> 00:27:41,910
Adele heard him, and asked if she was to go to school, saw Mademoiselle.

414
00:27:42,769 --> 00:27:44,610
Yes, he replied.

415
00:27:45,550 --> 00:27:47,330
Absolutely saw Mademoiselle.

416
00:27:48,150 --> 00:27:53,349
For I am to take Mademoiselle to the moon, and there I shall seek a cave in one of

417
00:27:53,351 --> 00:27:58,510
the white valleys among the volcano tops, and Mademoiselle shall live with me there,

418
00:27:59,449 --> 00:28:00,449
and only me.

419
00:28:01,209 --> 00:28:06,050
She will have nothing to eat, you will starve her, observed Adele.

420
00:28:07,690 --> 00:28:11,889
I shall gather Mademoiselle for her morning and night, the plains and

421
00:28:11,891 --> 00:28:14,529
hillsides in the moon are bleached with Mademoiselle.

422
00:28:15,550 --> 00:28:19,129
She will want to warm herself, what will she do for a fire?

423
00:28:20,669 --> 00:28:22,870
Fire rises out of the lunar mountains.

424
00:28:23,889 --> 00:28:26,245
When she is called, I'll carry her up to a

425
00:28:26,245 --> 00:28:29,811
peak and lay her down on the edge of a crater.

426
00:28:30,169 --> 00:28:35,769
Oh, curly Sarah Mel, poo comfortable, and her clothes they will wear out.

427
00:28:36,330 --> 00:28:37,550
How can she get new ones?

428
00:28:38,349 --> 00:28:40,269
Mr. Rochester professed to be puzzled.

429
00:28:41,569 --> 00:28:45,709
Him said he, What would you do, Adele?

430
00:28:46,129 --> 00:28:47,949
Cuddle your brains for an expedient.

431
00:28:48,769 --> 00:28:52,389
How would a white or a pink cloud answer for a gown, do you think?

432
00:28:53,129 --> 00:28:56,290
And one could cut a pretty enough scarf out of a rainbow.

433
00:28:57,669 --> 00:29:02,610
She is far better as she is, concluded Adele after musing some time.

434
00:29:03,569 --> 00:29:07,110
Besides, she would get tired of living with only you in the moon.

435
00:29:07,989 --> 00:29:10,910
If I were Mademoiselle, I would never consent to go with you.

436
00:29:12,010 --> 00:29:14,930
She has consented, she has pledged her word.

437
00:29:15,750 --> 00:29:19,809
But you can't get her there, there's no road to the moon, it is all air,

438
00:29:20,250 --> 00:29:21,870
and neither you nor she can fly.

439
00:29:23,110 --> 00:29:25,370
Adele, look at that field.

440
00:29:26,769 --> 00:29:32,550
We were now outside Thornfield gates, and bowling lightly along the smooth road

441
00:29:32,550 --> 00:29:39,410
to Milcoat, where the dust was well laid by the thunderstorm, and where the low

442
00:29:39,411 --> 00:29:45,769
hedges and lofty timbetries on each side glistened green and rain refreshed.

443
00:29:46,769 --> 00:29:52,250
In that field Adele, I was walking late one evening about a fortnight since,

444
00:29:52,889 --> 00:29:57,029
the evening of the day you helped me to make hay in the orchard meadows,

445
00:29:57,769 --> 00:30:04,690
and as I was tired with raking swathes, I sat down to rest me on a style,

446
00:30:05,610 --> 00:30:10,330
and there I took out a little book and a pencil, and began to write about a

447
00:30:10,330 --> 00:30:16,410
misfortune that befell me long ago, and a wish I had for happy days to come.

448
00:30:17,269 --> 00:30:21,809
I was writing away very fast, though daylight was fading from the leaf,

449
00:30:22,470 --> 00:30:26,610
when something came up the path and stopped two yards of me.

450
00:30:27,269 --> 00:30:31,809
I looked at it, it was a little thing with a veil of gossamer on its head,

451
00:30:32,650 --> 00:30:35,970
I beckoned it to come near me, it stood soon at my knee.

452
00:30:37,010 --> 00:30:42,750
I never spoke to it, and it never spoke to me in words, but I read its eyes,

453
00:30:43,610 --> 00:30:49,349
and it read mine, and our speechless colloquy was to this effect, it was a

454
00:30:49,351 --> 00:30:54,769
fairy, and come from elf land it said, and its errand was to make me happy.

455
00:30:55,669 --> 00:31:01,190
I must go with it out of the common world, to a lonely place, such as the moon,

456
00:31:01,370 --> 00:31:06,650
for instance, and it nodded its head towards her horn, rising over hay hill.

457
00:31:07,410 --> 00:31:11,489
It told me of the alabaster cave and silver veil where we might live.

458
00:31:12,430 --> 00:31:19,930
I said I should like to go, but reminded it as you did me, that I had no wings to fly.

459
00:31:20,169 --> 00:31:24,730
Oh, return the fairy, that does not signify, here is a talisman will remove

460
00:31:24,730 --> 00:31:28,849
all difficulties, and she held out a pretty gold ring.

461
00:31:29,750 --> 00:31:36,669
Put it, she said, on the fourth finger of my left hand, and I am yours, and you are

462
00:31:36,671 --> 00:31:41,510
mine, and we shall leave earth and make our own heaven yonder.

463
00:31:42,569 --> 00:31:49,190
She nodded again at the moon, the ring Adele is in my breaches pocket under the

464
00:31:49,190 --> 00:31:53,470
disguise of a sovereign, but I mean soon to change it to a ring again.

465
00:31:54,970 --> 00:31:57,190
But what has Mamoiselle to do with it?

466
00:31:57,910 --> 00:32:01,889
I don't care for the fairy, you said it was Mamoiselle you would take to the moon.

467
00:32:03,690 --> 00:32:10,589
Mamoiselle is a fairy, he said, whispering mysteriously, whereupon I told

468
00:32:10,591 --> 00:32:17,569
her not to mind his bad inage, and she, on her part, evinced a fund of

469
00:32:17,571 --> 00:32:24,190
genuine French scepticism, denominating Mr. Rochester on Vrymenta, and assuring

470
00:32:24,190 --> 00:32:29,209
him that she made no account whatever of his contife, and

471
00:32:29,211 --> 00:32:33,709
that du rest in the evade part de Faise équand m'élyanevate.

472
00:32:34,769 --> 00:32:39,391
She was sure they would never appear to him, nor ever

473
00:32:39,391 --> 00:32:42,629
give him rings, or offer to live with him in the moon.

474
00:32:44,069 --> 00:32:48,589
The hour spent at Milcoat was a somewhat harrassing one to me.

475
00:32:49,889 --> 00:32:53,830
Mr. Rochester obliged me to go to a certain silk warehouse.

476
00:32:54,750 --> 00:32:57,629
There, I was ordered to choose half a dozen dresses.

477
00:32:58,669 --> 00:32:59,790
I hated the business.

478
00:33:00,510 --> 00:33:02,290
I begged leave to defer it.

479
00:33:02,750 --> 00:33:05,330
No, it should be gone through with now.

480
00:33:06,809 --> 00:33:09,483
By dint of entreaties expressed in energetic

481
00:33:09,485 --> 00:33:12,290
whispers, I reduced the half dozen to two.

482
00:33:13,089 --> 00:33:16,849
These, however, he vowed he would select himself.

483
00:33:17,449 --> 00:33:21,529
With anxiety, I watched his eye rove over the gay stores.

484
00:33:22,529 --> 00:33:29,470
He fixed on a rich silk of the most brilliant amethyst die, and a superb pink satin.

485
00:33:29,669 --> 00:33:33,252
I told him in a new series of whispers, that he might

486
00:33:33,254 --> 00:33:36,830
as well buy me a gold gown and a silver bonnet at once.

487
00:33:37,629 --> 00:33:42,930
I should certainly never venture to wear his choice, with infinite difficulty,

488
00:33:43,569 --> 00:33:45,569
for he was stubborn as a stone.

489
00:33:46,389 --> 00:33:49,252
I persuaded him to make an exchange in favour

490
00:33:49,254 --> 00:33:52,491
of a sober black satin and pearl grey silk.

491
00:33:53,629 --> 00:33:57,042
It might pass for the present, he said, but

492
00:33:57,042 --> 00:34:00,129
he would yet see me glittering like a partair.

493
00:34:02,069 --> 00:34:09,190
Glad was I to get him out of the silk warehouse, and then out of a jewelers shop.

494
00:34:09,370 --> 00:34:12,029
The more he bought me, the more my cheek burned

495
00:34:12,031 --> 00:34:14,830
with a sense of annoyance and degradation.

496
00:34:15,690 --> 00:34:20,269
As we re-entered the carriage, and I sat back feverish and fact,

497
00:34:20,930 --> 00:34:25,769
I remembered what, in the hurry of events dark and bright, I had wholly forgotten.

498
00:34:26,629 --> 00:34:30,966
The letter of my uncle, John heir, to Mrs. Reed,

499
00:34:30,966 --> 00:34:36,029
his intention to adopt me and make me his legatee.

500
00:34:36,690 --> 00:34:43,069
It would indeed be a relief, I thought, if I had ever so small an independency.

501
00:34:43,830 --> 00:34:49,769
I never can bear being dressed like a doll by Mr. Rochester, or sitting like a second

502
00:34:49,771 --> 00:34:53,309
dane with the golden shower falling daily round me.

503
00:34:54,349 --> 00:34:59,069
I will write to Madera the moment I get home, and tell my uncle, John,

504
00:34:59,250 --> 00:35:04,930
I am going to be married, and to whom, if I had but a prospect of one day,

505
00:35:05,569 --> 00:35:08,828
bringing Mr. Rochester an accession of fortune,

506
00:35:08,828 --> 00:35:12,171
I could better endure to be kept by him now.

507
00:35:13,190 --> 00:35:17,870
And somewhat relieved by this idea, which I failed not to execute that day,

508
00:35:18,669 --> 00:35:24,550
I ventured once more to meet my masters and lovers eye, which most pertenaciously

509
00:35:24,550 --> 00:35:28,430
sought mine, though I averted both face and gaze.

510
00:35:29,690 --> 00:35:30,690
He smiled.

511
00:35:31,129 --> 00:35:35,410
And I thought his smile was such as a sultan might, in a blissful and fond

512
00:35:35,411 --> 00:35:39,449
moment, bestow on a slave his gold and gems had enriched.

513
00:35:40,209 --> 00:35:44,455
I crushed his hand, which was ever hunting mine, vigorously

514
00:35:44,455 --> 00:35:47,629
and thrust it back to him red with a passionate pressure.

515
00:35:48,989 --> 00:35:52,110
You need not look in that way, I said.

516
00:35:53,050 --> 00:35:58,389
If you do, I'll wear nothing but my old lowwood frocks to the end of the chapter.

517
00:35:59,870 --> 00:36:02,430
I'll be married in this lilac gingham.

518
00:36:03,589 --> 00:36:08,370
You may make a dressing gown for yourself out of the Pearl Grey silk, and an

519
00:36:08,370 --> 00:36:11,750
infinite series of waistcoats out of the black satin.

520
00:36:12,769 --> 00:36:13,769
He chuckled.

521
00:36:14,129 --> 00:36:15,209
He rubbed his hands.

522
00:36:16,129 --> 00:36:19,349
Oh, it is rich to see and hear her.

523
00:36:19,930 --> 00:36:20,930
He exclaimed.

524
00:36:21,510 --> 00:36:22,510
Is she original?

525
00:36:22,809 --> 00:36:23,809
Is she pecan?

526
00:36:24,110 --> 00:36:28,550
I would not exchange this one little English girl for the Grand Turks' whole

527
00:36:28,550 --> 00:36:31,930
saraglio, gazelle eyes, hoori forms and all.

528
00:36:33,510 --> 00:36:35,849
The Eastern allusion bit me again.

529
00:36:37,010 --> 00:36:40,381
I'll not stand you an inch in the stead of a saraglio,

530
00:36:40,383 --> 00:36:43,830
I said, so don't consider me an equivalent for one.

531
00:36:44,730 --> 00:36:50,669
If you have a fancy for anything in that line, away with you, sir, to the bazaars

532
00:36:50,671 --> 00:36:57,250
of Stamble without delay, and lay out in extensive slave purchases some of that

533
00:36:57,250 --> 00:37:01,230
spare cash you seem at a loss to spend satisfactorily here.

534
00:37:02,709 --> 00:37:07,072
And what will you do, Janet, while I'm bargaining for so

535
00:37:07,072 --> 00:37:10,730
many tons of flesh and such an assortment of black eyes?

536
00:37:12,190 --> 00:37:17,589
I'll be preparing myself to go out as a missionary, to preach liberty to them that

537
00:37:17,591 --> 00:37:21,750
are enslaved, your haram inmates amongst the rest.

538
00:37:22,669 --> 00:37:26,830
I'll get admitted there, and I'll stir up mutiny,

539
00:37:26,830 --> 00:37:30,411
and you, three-tailed Bashar as you are, sir.

540
00:37:30,910 --> 00:37:35,769
Shall in a trice find yourself fettered amongst our hands, nor will I,

541
00:37:35,930 --> 00:37:39,584
for one, consent to cut your bonds till you have signed a

542
00:37:39,584 --> 00:37:43,830
charter, the most liberal that despot ever yet conferred.

543
00:37:45,569 --> 00:37:48,089
I would consent to be at your mercy, Jane.

544
00:37:49,709 --> 00:37:52,122
I would have no mercy, Mr. Rochester, if you

545
00:37:52,122 --> 00:37:55,531
supplicated for it with an eye like that.

546
00:37:55,669 --> 00:38:01,730
While you looked so, I should be certain that whatever charter you might grant

547
00:38:01,730 --> 00:38:09,010
under coercion, your first act, when released, would be to violate its conditions.

548
00:38:09,930 --> 00:38:11,949
Why, Jane, what would you have?

549
00:38:12,849 --> 00:38:15,891
I fear you will compel me to go through a private

550
00:38:15,891 --> 00:38:18,809
marriage ceremony, besides that performed at the altar.

551
00:38:19,989 --> 00:38:24,730
You will stipulate, I see, for peculiar terms, what will they be?

552
00:38:26,470 --> 00:38:31,610
I only want an easy mind, sir, not crushed by crowded obligations.

553
00:38:32,790 --> 00:38:35,913
Do you remember what you said of Selin Varan,

554
00:38:35,913 --> 00:38:39,491
of the diamonds, the cashmiers you gave her?

555
00:38:40,169 --> 00:38:43,370
I will not be your English, Selin Varan.

556
00:38:44,410 --> 00:38:47,449
I shall continue to act as Adele's governess.

557
00:38:48,069 --> 00:38:51,930
By that, I shall earn my board and lodging and thirty pounds a year besides.

558
00:38:53,150 --> 00:38:58,089
I'll furnish my own wardrobe out of that money, and you shall give me nothing but,

559
00:38:58,809 --> 00:39:00,069
well, but what?

560
00:39:01,230 --> 00:39:02,250
Your regard.

561
00:39:03,190 --> 00:39:06,389
And if I give you mine in return, that debt will be quit.

562
00:39:07,550 --> 00:39:13,250
Well, for cool native impudence and pure innate pride, you haven't your equal,

563
00:39:13,970 --> 00:39:14,970
said he.

564
00:39:15,470 --> 00:39:18,069
We were now approaching Thornfield.

565
00:39:19,129 --> 00:39:21,470
Will it please you to dine with me today?

566
00:39:22,209 --> 00:39:24,610
He asked, as we re-entered the gates.

567
00:39:26,370 --> 00:39:27,830
No, thank you, sir.

568
00:39:28,830 --> 00:39:29,830
And what for?

569
00:39:30,569 --> 00:39:33,769
No, thank you, if one may inquire.

570
00:39:34,610 --> 00:39:38,650
I never have dined with you, sir, and I see no reason why I should now,

571
00:39:38,790 --> 00:39:44,449
till, till what, you delight in half -phrases, till I can't help it.

572
00:39:45,169 --> 00:39:47,805
Do you suppose I eat like an ogre or a ghoul,

573
00:39:47,805 --> 00:39:51,209
that you dread being the companion of my repast?

574
00:39:52,489 --> 00:39:56,108
I have formed no supposition on the subject, sir,

575
00:39:56,110 --> 00:39:59,050
but I want to go on as usual for another month.

576
00:40:00,269 --> 00:40:03,269
You will give up your governessing slavery at once.

577
00:40:04,510 --> 00:40:07,529
Indeed, begging your pardon, sir, I shall not.

578
00:40:08,389 --> 00:40:10,290
I shall just go on with it as usual.

579
00:40:10,970 --> 00:40:14,849
I shall keep out of your way all day, as I have been accustomed to do.

580
00:40:15,610 --> 00:40:20,290
You may send for me in the evening, when you feel disposed to see me,

581
00:40:20,910 --> 00:40:23,449
and I'll come then, but at no other time.

582
00:40:24,830 --> 00:40:29,250
I want to smoke, Jane, or a pinch of snuff, to comfort me under all this,

583
00:40:29,250 --> 00:40:35,430
pour me dawn a room condonce, as Adele would say, and unfortunately I have

584
00:40:35,430 --> 00:40:40,250
neither my cigar case, nor my snuff box, but listen, whisper.

585
00:40:41,370 --> 00:40:45,370
It is your time now, little tyrant, but it will be mine presently,

586
00:40:45,889 --> 00:40:50,930
and when once I have fairly seized you, to have and to hold, I'll just

587
00:40:50,930 --> 00:40:56,489
figuratively speaking, attach you to a chain like this, touching his watchguard.

588
00:40:57,709 --> 00:41:03,790
Yes, bonnie-wee thing, I'll wear you in my bosom, lest my jewel I should tine.

589
00:41:04,889 --> 00:41:10,129
He said this as he helped me to a light from the carriage, and while he afterwards

590
00:41:10,131 --> 00:41:15,230
lifted out Adele, I entered the house and made good of my retreat upstairs.

591
00:41:16,389 --> 00:41:19,389
He duly summoned me to his presence in the evening.

592
00:41:20,190 --> 00:41:23,557
I had prepared a occupation for him, for I was determined

593
00:41:23,559 --> 00:41:27,169
not to spend the whole time in a tet-a-tet conversation.

594
00:41:28,089 --> 00:41:30,169
I remembered his fine voice.

595
00:41:31,029 --> 00:41:32,129
I knew he liked to sing.

596
00:41:33,029 --> 00:41:34,330
Good singers generally do.

597
00:41:35,550 --> 00:41:40,870
I was no vocalist myself, and in his fastidious judgment, no musician either,

598
00:41:41,589 --> 00:41:44,550
but I delighted in listening when the performance was good.

599
00:41:45,910 --> 00:41:50,453
No sooner had twilight, that hour of romance began

600
00:41:50,453 --> 00:41:53,650
to lower her blue and starry banner over the lattice.

601
00:41:54,430 --> 00:41:58,067
Then I rose, opened the piano, and entreated

602
00:41:58,067 --> 00:42:01,790
him for the love of heaven to give me a song.

603
00:42:02,870 --> 00:42:08,010
He said I was a capricious witch, and that he would rather sing another time.

604
00:42:08,230 --> 00:42:10,870
But I avert that no time was like the present.

605
00:42:11,949 --> 00:42:13,230
Did I like his voice?

606
00:42:13,910 --> 00:42:15,809
He asked very much.

607
00:42:16,449 --> 00:42:21,510
I was not fond of pampering that susceptible vanity of his, but for once,

608
00:42:22,150 --> 00:42:27,029
and from motives of expediency, I would ensoothe and stimulate it.

609
00:42:28,529 --> 00:42:31,449
Then Jane, you must play the accompaniment.

610
00:42:32,970 --> 00:42:34,589
Very well, sir, I will try.

611
00:42:35,690 --> 00:42:40,309
I did try, but was presently swept off the stool and denominated a little bungler.

612
00:42:41,309 --> 00:42:46,190
Being pushed unceremoniously to one side, which was precisely what I wished.

613
00:42:46,830 --> 00:42:50,385
He usurped my place, and proceeded to accompany

614
00:42:50,387 --> 00:42:53,591
himself, for he could play as well as sing.

615
00:42:53,949 --> 00:42:55,889
I hide me to the window recess.

616
00:42:56,830 --> 00:43:02,269
And while I sat there, and looked out on the still trees and dim lawn, to a sweet

617
00:43:02,271 --> 00:43:04,889
air was sung in mellow tones the following strain.

618
00:43:06,050 --> 00:43:11,970
The truest love that ever-heart felt at its kindled core, did through each vein,

619
00:43:12,589 --> 00:43:15,790
in quicken start, the tide of being poor.

620
00:43:16,989 --> 00:43:21,504
Her coming was my hope each day, her parting was my pain,

621
00:43:21,504 --> 00:43:25,370
the chance that did her steps delay was ice in every vein.

622
00:43:26,269 --> 00:43:32,330
I dreamed it would be nameless bliss, as I loved loved to be, and to this object

623
00:43:32,330 --> 00:43:36,552
did I press, as blind as eagerly, but wide as

624
00:43:36,552 --> 00:43:39,671
pathless was the space that lay our lives between.

625
00:43:40,870 --> 00:43:47,129
And dangerous as the foamy race of ocean surges green, and haunted as a robber path

626
00:43:47,131 --> 00:43:50,902
through wilderness or wood, for might and right

627
00:43:50,902 --> 00:43:54,250
and woe and wrath, between our spirits stood.

628
00:43:54,889 --> 00:44:01,050
I dangers dared, I hindrance scorned, the omens did defy, whatever menaced,

629
00:44:01,169 --> 00:44:06,449
harassed, warned, I passed impetuous by, son sped my rainbow, fast as light,

630
00:44:07,069 --> 00:44:09,620
I flew as in a dream, for glorious rows upon

631
00:44:09,620 --> 00:44:13,010
my sight, that child of shower and gleam.

632
00:44:13,489 --> 00:44:19,110
Still bright on clouds of suffering dim, shines that soft solemn joy, nor care I

633
00:44:19,110 --> 00:44:21,989
now, how dense and grim disasters gather nigh.

634
00:44:22,750 --> 00:44:28,230
I care not in this moment, sweet, though all I have rushed over,

635
00:44:28,610 --> 00:44:35,089
should come on pinion, strong and fleet, proclaiming vengeance saw, though haughty

636
00:44:35,091 --> 00:44:39,949
hate should strike me down, right bar approach to me, and grinding might,

637
00:44:40,470 --> 00:44:43,669
with furious frown, swear endless enmity.

638
00:44:44,790 --> 00:44:50,150
My love has placed her little hand with noble faith in mine, and vowed that

639
00:44:50,150 --> 00:44:55,669
wedlock's sacred band, our nature shall entwine, my love has sworn with ceiling

640
00:44:55,671 --> 00:45:00,949
kiss, with me to live, to die, I have at last my nameless bliss,

641
00:45:01,629 --> 00:45:03,849
as I love, lover dem I.

642
00:45:04,930 --> 00:45:10,029
He rose and came towards me, and I saw his face all kindled, and his full falcon eye

643
00:45:10,031 --> 00:45:16,250
flashing, and tenderness and passion in every liniment, I quailed momentarily,

644
00:45:16,709 --> 00:45:17,709
then I rallied.

645
00:45:18,629 --> 00:45:24,410
Soft seen, daring demonstration I would not have, and I stood in peril of both,

646
00:45:25,209 --> 00:45:27,589
a weapon of defense must be prepared.

647
00:45:28,389 --> 00:45:32,050
I wetted my tongue, as he reached me, I asked

648
00:45:32,050 --> 00:45:35,690
with a sparity, whom he was going to marry now.

649
00:45:36,949 --> 00:45:40,430
That was a strange question to be put by his darling Jane.

650
00:45:41,169 --> 00:45:44,838
Indeed, I considered it a very natural and necessary

651
00:45:44,839 --> 00:45:48,730
one, he had talked of his future wife dying with him.

652
00:45:49,589 --> 00:45:51,589
What did he mean by such a pagan idea?

653
00:45:52,550 --> 00:45:56,650
I had no intention of dying with him, he might depend on that.

654
00:45:58,089 --> 00:46:02,519
Oh, all he longed, all he prayed for was that I

655
00:46:02,521 --> 00:46:06,629
might live with him, death was not for such as I.

656
00:46:08,069 --> 00:46:12,750
Indeed it was, I had as good a right to die when my time came as he had,

657
00:46:13,290 --> 00:46:16,750
but I should bide that time and not be hurried away in a suttie.

658
00:46:17,949 --> 00:46:22,730
Would I forgive him for the selfish idea and prove my pardon by a reconciling kiss?

659
00:46:23,910 --> 00:46:27,029
No, I would rather be excused.

660
00:46:27,830 --> 00:46:32,910
Here I heard myself apostrophized as a hard little thing, and it was added,

661
00:46:33,449 --> 00:46:36,300
any other woman would have been melted to marrow

662
00:46:36,302 --> 00:46:39,510
at hearing such stanzas crooned in her praise.

663
00:46:40,389 --> 00:46:47,790
I assured him I was naturally hard, very flinty, and that he would often find me so.

664
00:46:48,110 --> 00:46:53,309
And that moreover, I was determined to show him divers rugged points in my

665
00:46:53,311 --> 00:46:56,589
character before the ensuing four weeks elapsed.

666
00:46:57,129 --> 00:46:59,987
He should know fully what sort of a bargain he

667
00:46:59,989 --> 00:47:03,410
had made, while there was yet time to rescind it.

668
00:47:04,809 --> 00:47:07,150
Would I be quiet and talk rationally?

669
00:47:08,069 --> 00:47:12,065
I would be quiet if he liked, and as to talking

670
00:47:12,067 --> 00:47:15,491
rationally, I flattered myself I was doing that now.

671
00:47:16,690 --> 00:47:19,129
He fretted, pished and pshored.

672
00:47:20,510 --> 00:47:22,190
Very good, I thought.

673
00:47:23,430 --> 00:47:26,639
You may fume and fidget as you please, but this

674
00:47:26,639 --> 00:47:29,650
is the best plan to pursue with you, I am certain.

675
00:47:30,269 --> 00:47:34,449
I like you more than I can say, but I'll not sink into a bathos of

676
00:47:34,451 --> 00:47:37,203
sentiment, and with this needle of repartee

677
00:47:37,205 --> 00:47:40,211
I'll keep you from the edge of the gulf too.

678
00:47:40,830 --> 00:47:46,489
And moreover, maintained by its pungent aid, that distance between you and myself

679
00:47:46,491 --> 00:47:50,089
most conducive to our real mutual advantage.

680
00:47:52,089 --> 00:47:56,449
From less to more, I worked him up to considerable irritation.

681
00:47:57,349 --> 00:48:01,790
Then, after he had retired in Dungeon, quite to the other end of the room,

682
00:48:02,470 --> 00:48:05,769
I got up and saying, I wish you good night, sir.

683
00:48:06,589 --> 00:48:09,072
In my natural and wanted respectful manner,

684
00:48:09,074 --> 00:48:12,330
I slipped out by the side door and got away.

685
00:48:13,129 --> 00:48:18,129
The system thus entered on, I pursued during the whole season of probation,

686
00:48:18,989 --> 00:48:21,050
and with the best success.

687
00:48:21,989 --> 00:48:25,769
He was kept, to be sure, rather cross and crusty.

688
00:48:26,529 --> 00:48:32,250
But on the whole, I could see he was excellently entertained, and that a lamb

689
00:48:32,250 --> 00:48:37,129
-like submission and turtle-dove sensibility, while fostering his despotism

690
00:48:37,131 --> 00:48:40,940
more, would have pleased his judgment, satisfied

691
00:48:40,940 --> 00:48:44,650
his common sense, and even suited his taste less.

692
00:48:46,290 --> 00:48:51,750
In other people's presence, I was, as formerly, deferential and quiet,

693
00:48:52,669 --> 00:48:55,330
any other line of conduct being uncalled for.

694
00:48:56,050 --> 00:49:00,330
It was only in the evening conferences I thus thwarted and afflicted him.

695
00:49:01,050 --> 00:49:06,110
He continued to send for me punctually, the moment the clock struck seven.

696
00:49:07,169 --> 00:49:10,735
Though when I appeared before him now, he had no

697
00:49:10,737 --> 00:49:14,190
such honeyed terms as love and darling on his lips.

698
00:49:15,169 --> 00:49:20,110
The best words at my service were, provoking puppet, malicious elf,

699
00:49:20,830 --> 00:49:22,889
sprite, changeling, etc.

700
00:49:24,150 --> 00:49:29,830
For caresses, too, I now got grimaces, for a pressure of the hand, a pinch on the

701
00:49:29,830 --> 00:49:33,809
arm, for a kiss on the cheek, a severe tweak of the ear.

702
00:49:34,569 --> 00:49:35,569
It was all right.

703
00:49:36,129 --> 00:49:40,730
At present, I decidedly preferred these fierce favors to anything more tender.

704
00:49:41,470 --> 00:49:43,709
Mrs Fairfax, I saw, approved me.

705
00:49:44,330 --> 00:49:48,510
Her anxiety on my account vanished, therefore I was certain I did well.

706
00:49:49,250 --> 00:49:54,610
Meantime, Mr. Rochester affirmed I was wearing him to skin and bone, and

707
00:49:54,610 --> 00:49:59,569
threatened awful vengeance for my present conduct at some period fast-coming.

708
00:50:00,870 --> 00:50:03,370
I laughed in my sleeve at his menaces.

709
00:50:04,669 --> 00:50:08,580
I can keep you in reasonable check now, I reflected,

710
00:50:08,580 --> 00:50:11,809
and I don't doubt to be able to do it hereafter.

711
00:50:12,489 --> 00:50:17,370
If one expedient loses its virtue, another must be devised.

712
00:50:18,529 --> 00:50:21,669
Yet after all, my task was not an easy one.

713
00:50:22,389 --> 00:50:25,650
Often, I would rather have pleased than teased him.

714
00:50:26,550 --> 00:50:30,910
My future husband was becoming to me, my whole world, and more than the world,

715
00:50:31,589 --> 00:50:33,209
almost my hope of heaven.

716
00:50:34,889 --> 00:50:38,838
He stood between me and every thought of religion, as

717
00:50:38,838 --> 00:50:42,709
an eclipse intervenes between man and the broad sun.

718
00:50:43,970 --> 00:50:51,449
I could not, in those days, see God for his creature of whom I had made an idol.
